The Scripting Framework makes use of the Rhino (http://www.mozilla.org/rhino/)
JavaScript interpreter, available under the Mozilla Public License 2.0
(http://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/).

Rhino version: 1.7.7.2
Source archive: https://github.com/mozilla/rhino/releases/download/Rhino1_7_7_2_Release/rhino-1.7.7.2.zip
Checksum: (see external_deps.lst)

In addition, to support the debugging of scripts contained in OpenOffice.org
documents, we have modified the Java source files:
- GuiCallback.java (added exitInterrupt method)
- Main.java (added AOO-specific shortcut methods, nullified console I/O)
- Dim.java (added evalScriptWithReturn, changed default URL from "<stdin>" to "document")
- SwingGui.java (AOO-specific debugger GUI modifications)
- OfficeScriptInfo.java (new AOO-specific class)
- toolsrc/build.xml (excluded system rhino.jar from bootstrap classpath)
- DefiningClassLoader.java (modified class loading to check thread context class loader)

The Rhino source tarball is unpacked and patched with the modified code. The
Rhino Jar file (js.jar) is then built and delivered to the solver. The file
rhino1_7_7_2.patch contains the changes made in order to build Rhino. The patch
was generated using the command: diff -wurN

Java 8 compatibility: build.properties sets target-jvm and source-level to 1.8.
Ant-based build is preserved.
ES6 is the default language mode (Context.VERSION_ES6).
